	"machine_start_gcode": "PRINT_START EXTRUDER=[nozzle_temperature_initial_layer] BED=[bed_temperature_initial_layer_single] MATERIAL=[filament_type[initial_extruder]] MESH_MIN={adaptive_bed_mesh_min[0]},{adaptive_bed_mesh_min[1]} MESH_MAX={adaptive_bed_mesh_max[0]},{adaptive_bed_mesh_max[1]} PROBE_COUNT={bed_mesh_probe_count[0]},{bed_mesh_probe_count[1]} ALGORITHM=[bed_mesh_algo]\n\nG90               ; absolute XYZ mode\nM83               ; relative E mode\n\n; KAN-990: purge where the bed mesh probed. PURGE_LANE=1 has PRINT_START plan\n; a lane 6 mm in front of this print (behind it if the front has no room), off the notch,\n; and probes it with the mesh. PURGE_LINE draws the purge along it, or skips\n; it and says so when there was no room. Nothing here moves at purge height.\nSPEED_SLOW_PRE_PURGE_FOR_TPU MATERIAL=[filament_type[initial_extruder]]\nPURGE_LINE\nSPEED_NORMAL__POST_PURGE_FOR_TPU MATERIAL=[filament_type[initial_extruder]]\n\n; Lift clear of the front notch before the first travel. PURGE_LINE ends in its\n; lane at Z0.6, and the first travel goes straight to the first object, so at that\n; height it can cross the notch no-go box (x75-125, y0-34, Z 0..5), which needs\n; Z6 (C2 muon.m1-geometry v2, no_go.traverse_z).\nG1 Z6 F800\n\nM400                           ; wait for all moves to finish before continuing",
